there are three main reasons why grain  cannot be exported from ukraine at the  moment  firstly russia has taken control of some  of ukraine's major ports like mariupol  secondly there is a russian naval  blockade in the black sea both with  warships above the water and submarines  below it and thirdly the ukrainians and  probably the russians have mined the  black sea and so commercial shipping  companies are too nervous and they won't  be able to get the insurance to sell  their ships into the black sea ports  because of the threat coming from the  russian navy  ukraine produces around 12 of the  world's wheat 15 percent of the world's  corn and 50  of the world's sunflower oil and it is  exported across the world but primarily  to the middle east and africa countries  like lebanon egypt senegal on the west  coast of the african continent  these countries rely heavily on  ukrainian grain exports if 20 million  tons of grain  is not exported  from ukraine silos in the next three  months  then this year's crop will start to rot  and that would be a disaster the world  food programme has already said that it  is stopping giving food to hungry  children so they can divert it to  starving children it is a situation that  is deteriorating very rapidly indeed and  will get  worse quickly over the next few months  if nothing is done about it  the eu is looking at some alternative  routes out of ukraine and they have  asked that border crossings are sped up  when shipments arrive at customs but  none of the alternative options are  perfect  ukraine uses soviet era rail gauges that  are not compatible with european  railways  taking it by road is slow and cumbersome  and the options of canal routes into  countries like romania  also demand huge resources  i'm really anxious i mean  the only option is to get  the grain out of ukraine is through the  black sea porch they have to be open  that's the only option  there is a reason why ukraine's grain  gets shipped by sea  and that is because it is the most  efficient and the quickest way of  getting it around the world
 

